# SC2312: a command substitution used as an argument, or inside a test,
# discards the status of the command it runs. A check written that way
# passes when the command printed the right answer and then failed, or
# failed with nothing when nothing is the answer it wants. Assign the output
# first and test the status, or, where masking is intended, disable it on
# that command with a reason. SC2155, its counterpart for local and export,
# is on by default and stays on.
#
# Shellcheck cannot inspect command strings sent to another shell; review
# those strings for masked statuses too.
enable=check-extra-masked-returns
